# MoodBored — Visual Mood Board

When the user mentions moodboard, mood board, visual board, brand board, or design exploration, use MoodBored.

## Setup

```bash
cd /Users/x.hyperdex/OpenCodeApps/MoodBored
npm run dev   # http://localhost:5173
```

## MCP Tools (stdio)

Connect to `mcp/mcp-server.ts` via stdio. Key tools:

- `get_board` — read the board
- `add_items` — add notes, images, palettes, fonts, gradients, links, videos, containers
- `search_items` / `semantic_search` — find items by text or meaning
- `arrange_items` — grid/stack/spiral layout
- `clear_board` — wipe everything

## REST API

```
POST /api/boards                          — create board
POST /api/board/:id/items                 — add items
GET  /api/board/:id/search?q=             — text search
GET  /api/board/:id/semantic?q=           — semantic search
```

## Item format

```json
{"kind":"note","text":"...","purpose":"...","tags":["..."],"pos":{"x":100,"y":200}}
{"kind":"image","description":"...","source":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-XXX?w=800","tags":["..."]}
{"kind":"palette","label":"My Colors","colors":[{"hex":"#FF6B35","label":"Orange"}]}
```

All items accept `purpose`, `importance`, `tags`, `pos`, `size`.

## Rule: always populate the board

When the user describes anything visual, immediately add items via MCP or REST. Don't just discuss — create the board content. Use real Unsplash image URLs. Every response should add 2–8 items.
